1. d3 ( 1. e3 d5 2. d4 Nf6 3. c4 e6 4. Nc3 Be7 5. Nf3 O-O ) ( 1. a3 d5 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nf3 e6 4. e3 Be7 ) ( 1. h3 d5 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nf3 e6 4. c4 Be7 ) ( 1. Nh3 d5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 e6 4. O-O Be7 ) ( 1. a4 d5 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nf3 e6 4. e3 Be7 ) ( 1. h4 d5 { Takes the centre. Against every odd first move Black plays the same pawn to d5 and then the usual setup. } 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nf3 e6 4. Bg5 Be7 )
1... d5 { Takes the centre straight away. White's first move did little, so Black takes the space. }
2. Nf3 Nf6 { Develops and watches e4, the square White's pawns are heading for. }
3. g3 e6 { The usual setup: backs up d5 and opens the bishop on c8. }
4. Bg2 Be7 5. Nbd2 O-O 6. e4 c5 { Strikes at d4 and takes space; next come ...Nc6 and ...Re8. } *
